From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:14:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tests: the cases of fixes 98-105

152_gnu_extensions: an alias to a static function defined later without
a forward declaration, __auto_type of a const; 155_x86_inline_asm: a
forward jecxz/jrcxz and loop (8-bit relocations through tcc's linker on
both targets), "X" on i386, "i" operands of unsigned int, unsigned char
and unsigned short printed as gcc prints them; 157_i386_regparm_pic:
double, float and long double arguments, a variadic function and a
function pointer with a double argument under regparm(3); asmtest.S: ud1
in every size, movabs with small immediates, lar/lsl and segment-register
moves to 64-bit registers, ljmpw/lcallw through memory, and the data label
of the block renamed (var1 was defined twice) and made global, so the
GOTOFF relocations spell the same for GNU as and tcc.  The whole file now
disassembles like GNU as 2.47's except the two symbol names objdump picks
for the section starts.
